    /**
     * Makes sure a downloadable dataset is on disk and returns where it is.
     *
     * <p>For the tabular datasets ("diamonds", "california_housing") this is the CSV file. For the
     * image datasets it is a directory: "mnist" and "fashion_mnist" hold the four uncompressed
     * IDX files ({@code train-images-idx3-ubyte}, ...); "cifar10" holds {@code data_batch_1..5.bin} and
     * {@code test_batch.bin}; "cifar100" holds {@code train.bin} and {@code test.bin} (the binary versions);
     * "sudoku" holds Norvig's {@code easy50.txt}, {@code top95.txt} and {@code hardest.txt}.
     * "karate_club" holds the970-byte original ZIP, GML topology and source README;
     * every cached archive/member is checksum-verified. karate_club() reads34nodes/78edges.
     * "rebot_devarm" holds 38 pinned Seeed DevArm CAD/URDF/STL files and the
     * CERN-OHL-W-2.0 source license in their upstream relative directory layout.
     * DevArm verifies the size and SHA-256 of every cached file on every call;
     * changed files throw without replacement. Missing files are staged and verified
     * before publication. It uses the same offline/mirror/cache controls, and works
     * without the optional native data-preparation dependencies. Hashing uses memory
     * proportional to the largest source file (about 35 MB).
     * Approximate download sizes: diamonds 2.7 MB, california_housing 1.4 MB, MNIST 11 MB,
     * Fashion-MNIST 30 MB, CIFAR-10 163 MB, CIFAR-100 161 MB, sudoku 14 KB, DevArm 56 MB.
     *
     * <p><b>Example</b>
     *
     * <pre>{@code
     * const auto housing = dm::datasets::read_csv(dm::datasets::fetch("california_housing"));
     * }</pre>
     *
     * <p>For a complete CAD asset tree, use {@code dm::datasets::fetch("rebot_devarm")}.
     *
     * <p><b>References</b>
     *
     * <ul>
     * <li>Seeed reBot-DevArm source: https://github.com/Seeed-Projects/reBot-DevArm</li>
     * </ul>
     *
     * <p>Uses the C++ default for {@code directory = ""}.
     *
     * <p>C++: {@code std::string datamunge::datasets::fetch(const std::string & name, const std::string & directory = "")}
     *
     * @param name One of downloadable().
     * @return The local path of the CSV file or the dataset directory.
     * @throws NativeError.InvalidArgument for an unknown name. (C++ {@code std::invalid_argument})
     * @throws NativeException if files are missing and downloading is disabled or fails, or a download does not match its checksum. (C++ {@code std::runtime_error})
     * @see Datamunge#dataHome
     * @see Datamunge#downloadable
     * @see Datamunge#downloadFile
     * @see "karate_club"
     */
    public static String fetch(String name) {
        return Rosetta.asString(Rosetta.call(110, name));
    }

